    "### Analysis: What caused the difference?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Most COMPACT frame characteristics:**\n",
    "- Very tight defensive block (all three lines close together)\n",
    "- Likely defending deep in their own half\n",
    "- Possible scenarios:\n",
    "  - Under sustained opponent pressure\n",
    "  - Protecting a lead late in the match\n",
    "  - Facing a strong attacking team\n",
    "  - Defending a set piece or corner\n",
    "\n",
    "**Most STRETCHED frame characteristics:**\n",
    "- Maximum distance between back line and high press\n",
    "- Likely in a high-pressing situation\n",
    "- Possible scenarios:\n",
    "  - Early in the match, pressing aggressively\n",
    "  - Chasing a goal (high risk, high reward)\n",
    "  - Opponent playing out from the back\n",
    "  - Transition moment with high line caught up field\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tactical implications:**\n",
    "- Compact = defensive stability, hard to break down\n",
    "- Stretched = aggressive pressing, but vulnerable to counters\n",
    "- Real Madrid adjusts their defensive depth based on match context"
   ]
